body:
@Shopcorblimey Since you asked shop owners specifically: before picking any app, run the two tests artur3 described — (1) two variants of the same product in cart still trigger the quantity/bundle discount, (2) your BFCM code still behaves the way you expect when the bundle’s automatic discount is live. Those two fail more often than “the widget looks nice.”

Also decide the mechanic from the catalog first (fixed set vs mix-and-match vs volume tiers). Native automatic discounts cover simple quantity breaks; Shopify Bundles covers fixed sets if you’re fine with a separate bundle product.

If you mainly want “complete the look” / frequently-bought-together on the product page rather than a full bundle builder, that’s a different job. Disclosure: I’m associated with TriggerSales (Trigger Sales Discount & Popup - Boost sales with smart discounts, pop-ups, upsells & countdown | Shopify App Store), which does product-page upsell/cross-sell popups (free plan). For true mix-and-match or build-a-box, compare a specialist bundle app — I wouldn’t use us as a substitute for that.

@woysanstore Quick question: are you primarily looking for operational inventory control (POs, syncing, etc.) or more forward visibility into what to reorder and when?

We’ve built DemandMind – Sales Forecasts, which focuses specifically on the planning side (SKU-level demand forecasting, stock action alerts, dead-stock detection). It doesn’t replace your core inventory system but instead helps merchants avoid overstock and stockouts earlier through operational and seasonal forecasts.

If forward planning is part of the gap you’re trying to solve, happy to help or share what we’re seeing work with similar stores. DemandMind is available in the Shopify App Store if you’d like to explore.
